{"content":[{"c":["RAMOTH-GILEAD"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City lying in the Transjordan area of Gilead and probably identifiable with Tell Ramith, although the site of Tell el-Husn has also been suggested. Initially, biblical references pertain to Ramoth in Gilead (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.4.43","r":"Deut.4.43","rawR":"Deut.4.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.4.43","value":"Deut.4.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 4:43"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.20.8","r":"Josh.20.8","rawR":"Josh.20.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.20.8","value":"Josh.20.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 20:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.38","r":"Josh.21.38","rawR":"Josh.21.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.38","value":"Josh.21.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:38"},"), while later it is called Ramoth-gilead. Combined names were used to avoid confusion with cities of the same name in other locations."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Ramoth-gilead, a possession of the tribe of Gad, first appears in the biblical narrative as one of three Transjordan cities of refuge (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.4.43","r":"Deut.4.43","rawR":"Deut.4.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.4.43","value":"Deut.4.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 4:43"},") later included in the six cities of refuge for all Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.20.8","r":"Josh.20.8","rawR":"Josh.20.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.20.8","value":"Josh.20.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 20:8"},"). It was allotted to the Merarites as one of 48 Levitical cities (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.38","r":"Josh.21.38","rawR":"Josh.21.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.38","value":"Josh.21.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:38"},") and was most likely located along the King’s Highway, which transversed that area."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["During the time of Solomon, Ramoth-gilead enjoyed a place of prominence as the central city in his sixth administrative district and the residence of Ben-geber, chief officer of that district (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.13","r":"1Kgs.4.13","rawR":"1Kgs.4.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.13","value":"1Kgs.4.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:13"},"). After the division of the kingdom, this border town was taken by the Arameans and became a site of contention between Israel and Aram. King Ahab’s final battle began with his desire to retake Ramoth-gilead. In seeking to convince his ally Jehoshaphat, king of Judah, to support him in this maneuver, he produced many prophets who spoke favorable and victorious words to the king (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.22.1-53","r":"1Kgs.22.1-53","rawR":"1Kgs.22.1-53","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.22.1-53","value":"1Kgs.22.1-53"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.18.1-34","r":"2Chr.18.1-34","rawR":"2Chr.18.1-34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.18.1-34","value":"2Chr.18.1-34"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 18"},"). Unconvinced, Jehoshaphat inquired of the word of the Lord through Micaiah, a prophet of the Lord, who warned of impending disaster. The message was ignored and Ahab was killed at Ramoth-gilead. Ahab’s son Joram also fought with Aram here and was wounded in battle (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.8.29","r":"2Kgs.8.29","rawR":"2Kgs.8.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.8.29","value":"2Kgs.8.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 8:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.22.6","r":"2Chr.22.6","rawR":"2Chr.22.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.22.6","value":"2Chr.22.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 22:6"},"; also called Ramah). Shortly thereafter, Elisha sent one of the sons of the prophets to Ramoth-gilead, where he anointed Jehu to be king over Israel (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.9.1-14","r":"2Kgs.9.1-14","rawR":"2Kgs.9.1-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.9.1-14","value":"2Kgs.9.1-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 9:1-14"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Cities of Refuge"},"; ",{"href":"?item=LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Levitical Cities"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"RamothGilead","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 4:43","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.4.43","rawQueryValue":"Deut.4.43","sourceRefExact":"Deut.4.43"},{"anchorText":"Jos 20:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.20.8","rawQueryValue":"Josh.20.8","sourceRefExact":"Josh.20.8"},{"anchorText":"21:38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.38","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.38","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.38"},{"anchorText":"Dt 4:43","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.4.43","rawQueryValue":"Deut.4.43","sourceRefExact":"Deut.4.43"},{"anchorText":"Jos 20:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.20.8","rawQueryValue":"Josh.20.8","sourceRefExact":"Josh.20.8"},{"anchorText":"21:38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.38","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.38","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.38"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.13","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.13","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.13"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.22.1-53","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.22.1-53","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.22.1-53"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.18.1-34","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.18.1-34","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.18.1-34"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 8:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.8.29","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.8.29","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.8.29"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 22:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.22.6","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.22.6","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.22.6"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 9:1-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.9.1-14","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.9.1-14","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.9.1-14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3713554ffabfa86c2a3070d203ac5bc032ac340d0eef47623b2753e6deb3d8fb","sourceItemName":"RamothGilead","sourceItemOrder":48,"sourceMember":"Articles/R.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"RamothGilead","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Ramoth-Gilead","title":"Ramoth-Gilead","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}